%[text] %[text:anchor:T_76D33CB4] # Power Converter Circuit and Control Design with Simscape
%[text] Power converters are building blocks for electrification applications such as motor drives, chargers, automobiles, aerospace, distributed generation, renewable, battery energy storage systems, and consumer appliances.
%[text] This repository helps you design and simulate modern power converters and control algorithms. This repository contains eight design solutions: the grid-forming converter, the LLC converter, the dual active bridge converter, the bidirectional CLLC converter, the totem-pole boost PFC converter, the boost PFC converter, the interleaved boost PFC converter, and the non-isolated DC-DC converter.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] **Key words:** Power Converter, Grid-Forming Converters, Virtual Synchronous Machine, Droop Control, Virtual Impedance, Fault Ride Through, LLC Converter, Dual Active Bridge Converter, CLLC Converter, Bi-Directional Converter, Totem-Pole Boost PFC, Power Factor Correction, Bridgeless PFC, Boost PFC, Interleaved Boost PFC, Average Current Mode Control, 2P2Z compensator, Resonant converter
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_4af3] ## Design and Analysis of Grid-Forming Converter
%[text] The shift from synchronous machines to power electronics-based converters has introduced challenges like reduced system inertia and limited short-circuit current capacity. Traditional grid-following (GFM) converter control, which depends on grid measurements and PLL, cannot fully address these issues. GFM converters provide a better solution by emulating the inertia, damping, fault current, and power control capabilities of synchronous machines through control strategies that mimic their dynamic response.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C2DCF662] This figure shows a GFM converter connected to a typical network with renewable sources, a load, and a utility grid.
%[text] ![](text:image:1500)
%[text] The GFM design solution shows you how to develop and test a grid-forming (GFM) converter control. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Design a generic GFM converter and analyze its transient response.
%[text] - Implement an alternative inertia emulation technique to enhance stability.
%[text] - Configure control loops for flexible tuning and performance optimization.
%[text] - Apply different current-limiting methods for safe operation under fault conditions.
%[text] - Adapt the design to a wide range of network strengths.
%[text] - Verify conformance to grid codes \[[1](internal:M_EB223F76)\]. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('GridFormingConverterMain')) to open the main live script for the grid-forming converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:7058)
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_ED7FB925] ### Standard Test Scenarios for Grid-Forming Converters 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_419D4B21] This GFM design solution studies the performance of a GFM converter in test scenarios from the grid code standard GC0137 \[[1](internal:M_EB223F76)\]. This figure shows the GFM converter test scenarios found in the grid code standard GC0137 \[[1](internal:M_EB223F76)\]. The standard requires stable operation during grid disturbances, including changes in system frequency, phase, and voltage.
%[text] ![](text:image:90ce)
%[text] ## Design of LLC Resonant Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a full-bridge LLC resonant converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop an LLC converter that meets your specifications.
%[text] - Plot gain curves for various load conditions, quality factors, and inductor ratios.
%[text] - Fine-tune the converter by adjusting the quality factor and inductor ratio to achieve the required performance.
%[text] - Apply a time-domain simulation method to linearize the plant for control design.
%[text] - Design and tune the compensator in the controller to meet control performance requirements.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('LLCResonantConverterFullBridgeMain')) to open the main live script for the LLC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:9fed)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:6e05)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Bi-Directional CLLC Resonant Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a bi-directional full-bridge CLLC resonant converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop a CLLC converter that meets your specifications for both forward and reverse power flow.
%[text] - Plot the forward and reverse gain curves for various load conditions, quality factors, and inductor ratios.
%[text] - Fine-tune the converter by adjusting the quality factor and inductor ratio to achieve the required performance in both directions.
%[text] - Apply a time-domain simulation method to linearize the plant for control design.
%[text] - Design and tune the compensator in the controller to meet control performance requirements.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('CLLCBiDirectionalResonantConverterMain')) to open the main live script for the CLLC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:c101)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:c102)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Dual Active Bridge Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze an isolated bidirectional full-bridge dual active bridge (DAB) DC-DC converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop a DAB converter that meets your voltage, power, and switching-frequency specifications.
%[text] - Size the power stage, including the turns ratio, series inductance, and magnetizing inductance, under single-phase-shift (SPS) modulation.
%[text] - Plot the SPS power-transfer curves and verify zero-voltage switching (ZVS) across the operating envelope.
%[text] - Regulate the converter in constant-voltage or constant-current mode for onboard battery-charging applications.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('DualActiveBridgeConverterMain')) to open the main live script for the DAB converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:da01)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:da02)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Totem-Pole Boost PFC Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a bridgeless totem-pole boost power factor correction (PFC) converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop a totem-pole boost PFC converter that meets your input voltage, output power, and switching-frequency specifications.
%[text] - Size the boost inductor and the output capacitor from the allowed current ripple and the output hold-up requirement.
%[text] - Verify the peak inductor current and continuous conduction mode across the input voltage and load range.
%[text] - Select the fast-leg and slow-leg devices, and apply catalog parts that meet the required ratings.
%[text] - Shape the input current by using cascaded voltage and current control, and measure the input current harmonics and total harmonic distortion.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('TotemPoleBoostPFCMain')) to open the main live script for the totem-pole boost PFC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:tp01)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:tp02)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Boost PFC Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a single-phase boost power factor correction (PFC) converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop a boost PFC converter that meets your input voltage, output power, and switching-frequency specifications.
%[text] - Size the boost inductor and the DC-bus capacitor from the allowed current ripple and the output hold-up requirement.
%[text] - Verify the peak inductor current and continuous conduction mode across the input voltage and load range.
%[text] - Select the boost-leg and rectifier-bridge devices, and apply catalog parts that meet the required ratings.
%[text] - Shape the input current by using average-current-mode control, and measure the input current harmonics and total harmonic distortion.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('BoostPFCMain')) to open the main live script for the boost PFC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:bp01)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:bp02)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Interleaved Boost PFC Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a two-leg interleaved boost power factor correction (PFC) converter. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop an interleaved boost PFC converter that meets your input voltage, output power, and switching-frequency specifications.
%[text] - Size the per-leg boost inductors and the DC-bus capacitor, and verify how interleaving cancels the input current ripple.
%[text] - Verify the peak leg current and continuous conduction mode across the input voltage and load range.
%[text] - Select the per-leg boost devices and the shared rectifier bridge, and apply catalog parts that meet the required ratings.
%[text] - Shape the input current by using average-current-mode control with phase-shifted carriers, and balance the two leg currents.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('InterleavedBoostPFCMain')) to open the main live script for the interleaved boost PFC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:ip01)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:ip02)
%[text] ## Design and Analysis of Non-Isolated DC-DC Converter
%[text]  This design solution helps you design and analyze a non-isolated DC-DC converter, shipped as a synchronous boost. The design solution helps you to:
%[text] - Develop a non-isolated DC-DC converter that meets your input voltage range, output voltage, output power, and switching-frequency specifications.
%[text] - Size the inductor and the output capacitor for any of the six buck, boost, and buck-boost topologies, with or without a synchronous switch.
%[text] - Verify the peak inductor current and the continuous conduction boundary across the input voltage and load range.
%[text] - Select the switch and freewheeling diode devices, and apply catalog parts that meet the required ratings.
%[text] - Regulate the output voltage by using a cascaded voltage and current controller with anti-windup limiting and gate dead time.
%[text] - Estimate power loss in each component of the converter and calculate the overall efficiency by using support functions. \
%[text] [Click here](matlab:openMainScript('NonIsolatedDCDCMain')) to open the main live script for the non-isolated DC-DC converter design solution.
%[text] ![](text:image:nd01)
%[text] 
%[text] ![](text:image:nd02)
